WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.901
[music playing]

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:03.636
 Ryan, Steve, congratulations.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:06.539
You guys have earned your
spot in the final round

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.008
of this competition.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.509
You came here, you made
beautiful blades out of scraps,

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.244
and now it's time to send
you back to your home

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:15.414
forges to recreate this
iconic weapon from history.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.483
[music playing]

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:20.153
The nimcha.

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:22.288
Pay attention to
details, bladesmiths.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.190
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.291
- Good luck.
- Good luck.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:26.426 line:14%
[music playing]

00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:29.995
STEVE: We're in Omaha, Illinois.

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.497
It's raining outside.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.666
It's a good day to work in
the shop building our nimcha.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:36.469
I'm going to put the fullers
in before I start forging.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:42.642
[music playing]

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.043
My point is going good.

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:45.912
I got it pretty
close to what I want.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:49.749
My forge is not real long, and
while I'm forging this blade,

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.284
it wants to warp.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.986
I don't think I accounted
for the length of this blade,

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:54.921
and the weight.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.522
The ends want to hang out.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:59.159
I've got a lot of steel there,
a lot of stuff to manage.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.228
That's going to be the challenge
to keep that under control.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.897
Got my blade shaped out,
pretty close to parameters,

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.432
so day one in the books.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.467 line:14%
[music playing]

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:11.637
RYAN: Back at the home
forge, ready to start

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.105
beating out this nimcha.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.174
I've never made
anything this big.

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:17.343
I'm used to making three
to five inch skinners,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:21.147
so it's going to be a difficult
build to keep it straight.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:24.316
I have chosen a piece
of 5160 spring steel.

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:27.253
I'm very familiar with it,
and it holds a good edge.

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:29.388
As I'm beveling this
thing, the natural curve

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:32.124
is coming into this metal
and making it curve for me.

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:34.860
It flowed in, and
it just worked out.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:37.062
I feel good at the
end of day one.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:40.433
My blade is forged out,
parameters are met on it.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.170
Tomorrow, I just got to go
in and go full throttle.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.005
STEVE: It's
beginning of day two,

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:48.274
so we're going to get after it.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.576
Working on my guard
right now, trying

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:53.279
to get a guard straightened
out of a railroad spike,

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.281
and using this old hammer.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.984
It needs some maintenance,
so we're just going to make

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:01.387
it work the best we can.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.889
Oh, [bleep].

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:07.293
I think this belt's hitting
this flywheel, knocking it off.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.761
This got me kind of behind.

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:12.498
The hammer just wasn't
performing like it should.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:13.366
Oh, I see.

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:15.702
That's what that is, duct tape.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.069
Throw some more tape on that.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.772
[music playing]

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:20.607
Let's see.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:25.378
That seemed to
work a lot better.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:28.947
End of day two, I feel pretty
good, got my guard done today.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.282
Got it fit up.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.551
I'm pretty happy with
how it turned out.

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:35.220 line:8%
RYAN: I'm pretty excited of
where I finished up yesterday.

00:02:35.287 --> 00:02:36.755 line:14%
I got all the forging done.

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:39.892
Today, I'm going to finish
grinding and put fullers in it

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:42.294
and get it ready for quenching.

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:44.229
I'm going to take a
lot of the mass out,

00:02:44.296 --> 00:02:46.064
but I will leave some
meat on the bones

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:47.867
so it doesn't warp
or twist on me.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.702
[music playing]

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.504
Everything's going smooth,
just like it's supposed to.

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:55.341
Now that the bevels are in,
I'm ready to go into quench.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.876
I'm a little nervous
about the quench,

00:02:56.942 --> 00:02:58.210
being the long blade like it is.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.879
There's a lot of things
that can go wrong.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.181
[music playing]

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.419
I didn't hear no tings or pings.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.221
I feel pretty good about
it, but we'll have to look

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:12.024
and see after it cools off.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:15.427
And we've got a straight blade.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:16.429
Perfect.

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:18.030
End of day two, I feel great.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.065
I got the blade quenched.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.566
I got the fullers put in it.

00:03:20.632 --> 00:03:23.235 line:8%
It's turning out to
be a beautiful blade.

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:25.204 line:14%
STEVE: Day three, feel good.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:28.073 line:14%
Right now, it's heat treat time.

00:03:28.173 --> 00:03:29.408
It's a little nerve wracking.

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:31.377
You put all this
work into something

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.846
and it all hinges
on this one moment.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.448
[music playing]

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:42.654
This is where
things could go bad.

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:43.155
[bleep]

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.490
[music playing]

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:50.429
Uh-oh, cover it
up with something.

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:54.233
Outside of the fireball in my
face, heat treat went well.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.869
I had some minor bends,
and I think I can clean

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.604
it up good on the grinder.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.040 line:8%
We're ready to start
on the handle tomorrow.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:04.844 line:8%
BRIAN: Today is a day four,
and also, it's my birthday.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.413
I've got to finish cleaning
the guard up on it,

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:10.015
fit it, put a pommel on it.

00:04:10.115 --> 00:04:11.517
My brain's running
100 miles an hour,

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:14.286
and I can't figure out how
to get this pommel to stay.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.655
After I sat back and I
figured out how to do it,

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:18.858
I threaded my tang and
screwed my pommel on.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.626
It's going to give enough
weight on the back side,

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.996
I think, to balance
this blade out.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:24.530
Now that everything's
glued together

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.431
and everything's
all constructed,

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:30.970
I go to finish sharpening
and polishing my blade.

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:33.706
Now ready to test it and
see what's it's going to do.

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:34.741
[music playing]

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.710
End of day four,
and I feel great.

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:40.112
The blade's done,
and I get a surprise

00:04:40.178 --> 00:04:41.647
birthday party from my family.

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:44.417
It makes me really happy,
just couldn't be a better day.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:47.453
I'm ready for competition.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.589
DOUG MARCAIDA: Bladesmiths,
welcome to the kill test.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.858
It's time to find out
what kind of lethal damage

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.459
your nimchas will do.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.696
I will take your weapon,
deliver some lethal blows

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.230
on this boar carcass.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.132
Ryan, you're up first.

00:04:59.232 --> 00:04:59.998
You ready for this?

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:01.167
 Make some barbecue cut.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:03.002
 All right, let's try.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:06.572
 Seeing the boar carcass,
I'm smiling from ear to ear.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.775
I wanted to see him cut a
boar carcass in half with it.

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:10.876
I know it's razor sharp.

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.578
[music playing]

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:30.929
 All right, Ryan,
I don't know what's

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:35.033
a bigger beast, the boar carcass
or your nimcha right here.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.669
This is a heavy sword.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:39.405
Everything about the weight
that you have on this

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:42.341
allows for a very,
very deep cut,

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.543
but it's a lot of work
because of the weight.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:48.647
It's very forward heavy,
but overall, it will kill.

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:49.615
 Thank you.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:50.650
 All right, Steve,
your turn, sir.

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:51.784
Are you ready?
- Yes, sir.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.853
 Let's do this.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.455
 I'm excited.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:58.491
Ryan's blade cut well, so I know
I've got some competition here.

00:05:58.558 --> 00:05:59.291
Mine better perform.

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:15.141
[music playing]

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:18.711
 All right, Steve, let's talk
about your nimcha right here.

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:22.615
First up, the handle
construction, it's smooth.

00:06:22.681 --> 00:06:25.784
It's not blocky, so I like that
you have it ovoid over there

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:27.086
and marries in.

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:30.456
Before I started testing,
your blade had a little bit

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.291
kick off to the side.

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:34.726
But after the test,
it stayed the same.

00:06:34.793 --> 00:06:38.597
Your edge, with a thinner
profile like that, cuts deep.

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:43.703
Also it is a much lighter
sword than your competitor's.

00:06:43.769 --> 00:06:45.138
I can control with every slash.

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:48.974
Overall, sir, your
blade feels good.

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:49.941
It will kill.

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:50.810
 Thank you, sir.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:56.415
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the strength

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:59.418
past, the pillar and pot chop.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.087
To test the strength and
durability of your edge

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:03.289
as well as the overall
construction of your nimchas,

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:05.558
I'll be chopping into
these pots and pillars.

00:07:05.624 --> 00:07:06.792
Remember this test
is all about what

00:07:06.858 --> 00:07:08.661
the targets do to your
blades and not what

00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:10.095
your blades do to the target.

00:07:10.195 --> 00:07:11.230
Ryan, you're up first.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:11.963
You ready for this?

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:12.732
 Tear it up.

00:07:12.799 --> 00:07:14.066
 All right, man.

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.669
BRIAN: I know I'm behind
the eight ball right now.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:19.905
I need to perform really well
in the strengthness test.

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:22.208
Hopefully, I'll pull back
up into line with him

00:07:22.274 --> 00:07:23.008
and be evened up.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:24.677
[music playing]

00:07:42.461 --> 00:07:44.063
 Well, Ryan, in
the strength test,

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.732
the edge that you have on
here took a slight roll.

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:50.336
Like, I can't see it so
much as I can feel it.

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:53.271
The rest of it is
really wicked sharp.

00:07:53.338 --> 00:07:55.441
It's still all in one piece.

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:56.175
Nice job.

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:57.510
 Thank you.

00:07:57.576 --> 00:07:58.711
 Steve, you're up next.
You ready for this?

00:07:58.778 --> 00:07:59.344
 Yes, sir.

00:07:59.444 --> 00:08:00.412
 All right, cool.

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:01.614
[music playing]

00:08:01.714 --> 00:08:03.215
STEVE: I feel pretty good.

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:05.517
I think my blade cut a little
better than Ryan's maybe,

00:08:05.584 --> 00:08:07.920
but he didn't have that
can't and flaw on his blade,

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:10.155
so I think I've got a blade
that will hold up to it.

00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:11.891
[music playing]

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:26.138
 [bleep], man.

00:08:26.205 --> 00:08:27.840
[music playing]

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:36.815
 Well, Steve, we
got a problem, man.

00:08:36.915 --> 00:08:38.984
When I picked this
sword up, I was excited.

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:41.753
It's nice, light, got
a good shape to it,

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:44.322
but looking at your
steel here, it's

00:08:44.389 --> 00:08:45.891
a really big grain in here.

00:08:45.991 --> 00:08:48.294
You really could have used more
thermal cycling, I'm guessing.

00:08:48.361 --> 00:08:50.296
I don't know how you
heat treated this,

00:08:50.396 --> 00:08:53.299
but however you did,
it ended up brittle.

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:54.534
[music playing]

00:08:58.837 --> 00:09:01.974
 Well, Steve, your blade has
suffered a catastrophic failure

00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:03.642
during our strength
test and can no

00:09:03.708 --> 00:09:05.511
longer continue with testing.

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:08.180
Therefore, I'd like to invite
you to shake our hands,

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:11.216
shake your competitor's hand,
and then please exit the forge.

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:12.651
[music playing]

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:13.852
 Congratulations, man.

00:09:13.952 --> 00:09:15.955
STEVE: I'm disappointed
my blade broke.

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:19.324
I didn't want to go out that
way, but it is what it is.

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:20.493
Thank you.

00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:22.061
I just must get my
heat treat wrong.

00:09:22.128 --> 00:09:24.330
Nobody's fault but my own.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.565
I didn't win the
competition, but I gained

00:09:26.665 --> 00:09:28.534
so much more than I lost here.

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:31.003
I'm going to walk away here
with my head held high,

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.706
and it's going to make me
a better bladesmith for it.

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:35.106
I've really learned a lot.

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:36.242
[music playing]

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:40.446
 Ryan, congratulations.

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:41.913
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:42.013 --> 00:09:44.216
and that is a title that
comes with a check--

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:45.451
go ahead, you can smile--

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:47.219
for $10,000, brother.

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:48.153
Good job.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.020
[applause]

00:09:49.087 --> 00:09:49.521
Come on.

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:51.223
 Thank you, sir.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:51.957
 Good job.

00:09:52.057 --> 00:09:53.125
 Thank you.

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:54.827
It's not how I wanted
to win this competition,

00:09:54.893 --> 00:09:57.096
but, you know, it is what it is.

00:09:57.196 --> 00:09:58.597
First thing I'm going
to do is hug and kiss

00:09:58.664 --> 00:10:01.300
my wife and love on the
kids and play with them

00:10:01.366 --> 00:10:02.701
and get right back in the forge.

00:10:02.767 --> 00:10:04.135
There's no sleep for the wicked.

00:10:04.236 --> 00:10:06.872
[music playing]

